  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building of Cooperative Babiri Barutumwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Coffee.Beneficiaries: 1606.Description: Cooperative Babiri Baruta Umwe is a coffee cooperative headquartered on Gatare hill, Kivyuka zone of Musigati Commune in Bubanza Province. The group seeks to improve the quantity and quality of coffee produced by its members and access a better market by constructing a warehouse and pre-drying warehouse, conducting trainings on good agricultural practices, post-harvest processing, and marketing. The group also seeks to improvement their management and leadership&apos;s capacity for organizational and financial management by hiring experienced staff (accountant, agronomist), and developing a business plan.</narrative>
  </description>
